const items0 = [["HG14-emuC", () => "The inner child, the guards, and the three inner adults\n\nYour inner child won\u2019t trust you right away. It\u2019s not going to be enough for you to meditate, say three nice sentences to the inner child and expect to have its trust. What\u2019s going to help your inner child to trust you is you, as a person that you are right now.\n\nIn this post I am going to talk about what you need to develop in yourself in order to be able to reparent your inner child. I\u2019m going to talk about it in terms of three aspects: your Nurturer, your Protector and your Leader/Guru, but I don\u2019t mean them as if there were really three people in you. It\u2019s you that needs to develop these qualities.\n\nAlso, your inner child\u2019s worth is not dependent on these qualities\u2026 It has its own worth, and its own qualities, like playing, being tender, not taking life too seriously, being creative and wondering at the world.\n\nWhen the adult role is not available yet\n\nThe problem is, that some people do not have access to their adult functions at will. Instead, they may go blank, access an inherited inner critic, or even more commonly \u2013 access a child part who may be playing at being an adult. Telling them to just access their adult is like telling them to just be able to fly.\n\nTo help these people access their adult functions, I recommend the following steps. Please note, the following is a bridge that I developed \u2013 while many of the steps have been shown to be effective, the entirety of the steps have not (to the best of my knowledge).\n\n- Access a witnessing position, if necessary. If you already know how to distinguish your internal positions, skip to the next step and access the adult position you need.\n\n- Borrow an adult function. You may \u201cborrow\u201d this from a safe adult in your life, a mentor, an older sibling, a future version of yourself, a spiritual figure, a value, or even a written plan. Borrow whatever you need \u2013 warmth, direction, etc.\n\n- Put on the adult hat as an apprentice. Now, in this position, figure out what you would want to say or do \u2013 and then do at least a part of that.\n\n- Return the adult hat, noticing what you borrowed and what you were able to do on your own (even if it\u2019s only 5%).\n\nThis is a borrowed figure, so you\u2019re still making the choice. The longer version of this exercise can be found in my Inner Child Self-Love Reparenting Guide .\n\nYou don\u2019t have to have trustworthy people in your history. Just imagine a good adult. See if you can imagine what they would say/do in your situation, with your history, limitations, options, etc. If you can\u2019t imagine good, imagine the least cruel thing you can. Once you\u2019ve found something good, try it, don\u2019t keep doing the exercise.\n\nIt can be helpful to use borrowing when you\u2019re in the adult position and not knowing what a decent adult would do, especially when it seems like any response will be retaliatory, defensive, collapsing, leaving, etc. Borrow a decent adult\u2019s response. You may still feel young when you do it, it\u2019s okay, you\u2019ll become an adult after you act like one.\n\nLet the child speak without handing over the steering wheel\n\nIt is possible to regress psychologically and allow those younger states to talk, but still maintain adult judgement. You don't have to turn that judgement over to someone else or literally become younger. You just get to tap into those feelings of wonder, play, sensation, vulnerability, need or whatever it is you feel you need less responsibility.\n\n\"It is okay for a younger part of me to talk. But I understand that the adult in me is always going to be here, evaluating, protecting me and stopping me if needed. I am not going to replace my adult judgement with any child state, guide, recording or person.\"\n\nThis way you get the benefits of being young; curiosity, spontaneity, play, sensation, the ability to state your needs, to feel easily etc without any of the negatives of being a child, like obeying, being helpless, being scolded, the lack of good judgement etc.\n\nLove doesn\u2019t have to wait for trust\n\nIf the younger position doesn\u2019t believe you love him/her yet, you can still love him/her. You can love him/her even if the trust position doesn\u2019t trust your promises yet, even if he/she remembers that you haven\u2019t been able to protect him/her yet.\n\nYou can start with something like, \u201cOkay. I believe that you don\u2019t believe me. I still love you though. It\u2019s okay if you don\u2019t love me yet. Tell me what doesn\u2019t feel safe to you.\u201d\n\nRespond to complaints by hearing the truth in them and by responding to them, as well as by providing the other evidence of love: preparing and serving meals, setting limits to protect him/her, taking him/her to appointments, keeping promises, admitting when you haven\u2019t been able to live up to your promises, etc. If the younger position attacks you in his/her mind, admit that you haven\u2019t been able to protect him/her yet, work on it, and let him/her know when you\u2019ve made a change. Show your love by not retaliating, but don\u2019t substitute not retaliating for loving the younger position.\n\nKeep in mind that the position that made the vow and the position that blames the child for not accepting the vow may be two separate positions, or they may be the same position, or they may be a blend. Don\u2019t go by chronological age.\n\nImagine that you are in court and the defendant is you, only a few years younger. Would it be of any value to try and understand why you did whatever it was you did? Would it help to try and appreciate what options you felt you had? Would any useful insight be gained by considering the consequences of your actions? Whilst acknowledging the harm you may have caused, and working to address and repair that harm, would simply punishing you make any difference to the person you were when you committed the offence?\n\nThe two-hand practice\n\nSo here is a simple easy little bit of body work that will help you get in touch with your inner child. All you have to do is place one hand in the center of your chest. Remember your heart is there and it's full of love. Now place your other hand just below that, at your solar plexis, that is where you can relate to your child.\n\nNow begin sending love down to your child from your heart and just notice what comes up for you. It doesn't matter if something comes up or not, if there is resistance come it with love, if you feel or see something come it with love. Just communicate with your child from your heart.\n\nNow remember when you do this, Love is on top and your child is on the bottom and you as the adult are right there with them.\n\nThe Nurturer\n\nOne of the most important things you can do as a Nurturer is to enjoy your children. To sit back and not feel like you have to move their feelings, but actually say to them, \u201cI\u2019m really glad you are here in this moment.\u201d Children need to be enjoyed, not just consoled when they are hurt.\n\n\u201cI know it\u2019s okay for you to feel the way you are feeling.\u201d\n\n\u201cI want you to know that I\u2019m here for you.\u201d\n\n\u201cRight now, you don\u2019t have to do anything.\u201d\n\n\u201cYou are not too much.\u201d\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s okay to be small. You can be small here with me.\u201d\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s okay to be angry. You can be angry here.\u201d\n\n\u201cIt\u2019s okay to be sad. You can be sad here.\u201d\n\n\u201cI\u2019m going to be here for you.\u201d\n\nThe Protector\n\nIdentify your protector and try to bring a bit of their warmth.\n\nThen set boundaries together - it can be anything from, 'I will leave that conversation', 'I will stop texting that person', 'I will eat today', 'I will get some sleep tonight', 'I will do x', or, 'I won't put you in the position of having to deal with x '.\n\nIt's important to note that lots of people do ICW but it's often fluffy brouhaha - they talk to their IC, but they don't actually do the things they need to in their adult life. So in order to build trust with your IC, you need to do the thing . And deal with the fallout if you don't.\n\nIf you can't bring any warmth to the Protector, that's okay, just work with them on doing protective things for your child. Make sure they are attainable. If you don't do them, work out why - was it fear, exhaustion, lack of skills, lack of X, poor planning, etc.? Also, make sure that doing them is actually helpful - don't just be ticking things off a list.\n\nThe Leader, Guide, or Guru\n\nWorking with the Leader function, who provides direction. You can give it the name you like: Leader, Guide, Guru, Wise One, Sage, Inner Teacher, Director, Higher Adult, etc.\n\nInvite it to give direction in an effective way, not in a way that expects you to be perfectly disciplined and not have any needs. Ask it to help you find a way to do the adult thing and ask for help, express a preference, allow a safe person to see your imperfections, etc. Find ways to get your need for closeness met without punishing the other person for needing space. Etc.\n\nAffirmations to support the Leader may include: \u201cWe are not only here to feel good.\u201d \u201cWe are here to become whole.\u201d \u201cWe are here to belong to life itself, not only to people who approve of us.\u201d \u201cWe are here to serve truth, beauty, love, God, source, nature, universe, dharma, Tao, the benefit of all beings.\u201d Etc.\n\nBegin working with the adult function, perhaps beginning with protection, then warmth. Be sure that the direction serves your child\u2019s growth, but doesn\u2019t deprive your child of necessary care, play, support, etc.\n\nWorking with protectors\n\nIf this language is familiar to you, feel free to use it.\n\nMost people assume when approaching their inner child that the first thing they\u2019ll encounter is\u2026their inner child.\n\nBut more often than not, what you actually experience is numbness, cynicism, anger, hunger, the sudden urge to check your phone, a sexual urge, mental planning, sleepiness, dissociation, or the simple thought that \u201cthis is stupid\u201d. These are all common manifestations of protectors.\n\nOne of the most important protectors to become aware of when approaching your inner child is your inherited parent. This is the voice of your parent(s) that you internalized as a child, based on how they treated you. This is not the same as your inner adult (Nurturer, Protector, Leader/Guru) that you will eventually build up. Often this inherited parent acts as a critic or warden, telling your inner child not to cry, not to be \u201cneedy\u201d, not to embarrass them, not to be too independent, etc. So when you begin talking to your child in a new, loving way, this voice may jump in to say that what you\u2019re doing is \u201cfake\u201d.\n\nIt\u2019s okay, I see what you\u2019re doing. Can I ask you what you\u2019re afraid would happen if you let this go?\n\nNow be patient, and listen. It may be that they\u2019re afraid that you\u2019ll fall for your bullshit again, or that you\u2019ll spiritualize this issue, or feel your pain, or forgive someone too early, or believe your fantasies again, or leave them hanging once the therapy session is over.\n\nNow, thank the protective part, and ask them what they need from you to feel 1% safer.\n\n99% of the time, the answer will be some non-spiritual thing like maintaining a boundary, doing a certain task, eating properly, holding back from sending a text, or sleeping, or reaching out to a therapist, or acknowledging that you do, in fact, owe someone money.\n\nProtection that knows when to stop scanning\n\nDoes anyone here practice the following sequence to \u201cembody\u201d Protector?\n\n(1) orient self (look around, feel support, etc.),\n\n(2) assess situation (what do you know, not know, need to check out?),\n\n(3) differentiate between actual/real dangers, uncertainty, past dangers or imagined dangers,\n\n(4) set boundaries (just one, proportional to danger level; move, stop, delay, ask, leave, get support, etc.),\n\n(5) verify sufficient safety (based on reality), and finally\n\n(6) stand down and rest.\n\nSeems to me that this would be a \u201cmature\u201d Protector. For example, it wouldn\u2019t be afraid to say, \u201cI don\u2019t know\u201d, or to ask another human being, or to delay interpreting what\u2019s going on, or to use a no-trance practice. I want to be able to \u201cdo\u201d this. I am learning discernment and to quit scanning the room after taking appropriate action.\n\nInner child reparenting\n\nClient, I want to talk about the connection between the reparenting therapy you are doing, and the self hypnosis. I think it can be a perfect fit. So, while you are in hypnosis, you might summon the child (this can be any age, image, posture, voice, memory, emotion, vulnerable self, or no child at all. If there is no child, just work with whatever protector you do have, either in the form of a sensation, feeling, or preference).\n\nIf there is a child that appears, don\u2019t feel like you have to do anything with them. Just be with them.\n\nSee if you can tell the child: \u201cLittle one, you don\u2019t have to do anything for me, you don\u2019t have to tell me anything, you don\u2019t even have to be healed. You don\u2019t have to impress me. Just tell me if there\u2019s something you need to help you feel less alone in this world.\n\nIt can be anything. Need to warm yourself by a fire? need to play? need protection? need to grieve? need to be angry? need food? rest? a boundary? a relationship? need to stop fantasizing? need to stop working so hard? need me to keep a promise to you for one day?\n\nDon\u2019t rush the repair\n\nFind a younger you /protector/feeling/signal in your body that needs tending to and then:\n\nPrepare yourself to do the tending (Get yourself into a place where you have time, privacy, support etc. Be as adult as you can)\n\nAsk for permission to move closer or what is needed (warmth, space, words, silence, no contact etc)\n\nDo something to meet one of the needs you find when you move closer. Don\u2019t try to fix it all.\n\nWait a while for the effect of what you have done to sink in.\n\nReconnect with that part of you ( don\u2019t expect it to become one with you, go away, or be happy, just connect if it wants to)\n\nRest a while and then reassess to see how things are now.\n\nYour aim is not to make it all good as new but good as you. Feel free to change the language if the part talk is not useful, think signal, feeling, younger you or anything that helps you connect with the issue\n\nPlay and rest still need an adult present\n\nIt is important for reparenting to remember to have fun. It's really okay to let your younger states enjoy playing with things that interest them. Touch textures, draw, move your body, talk to your plushie in a different voice, as long as you can keep reality testing intact and remember that you are not actually a child/pet/doll/whatever and are not owned, it's okay to recover your play ability.\n\nResting without being helpless Sometimes you just need to rest, but you don't\u2026 [...]\n\nNon-dominant hand dialogue\n\nIf speaking or visualization doesn\u2019t work, try writing. Have your non-dominant hand write as your child/protector (even if your handwriting looks a little awkward), and have your dominant hand answer as you. For example, your non-dominant hand might write, \u201cI don\u2019t trust you.\u201d Answer with your dominant hand, \u201cI hear that you don\u2019t trust me, but I love you, and I want to know where I\u2019ve let you down. I won\u2019t ask you to trust me, but I want to hear you out and make one promise to you that I will keep today.\u201d Your non-dominant hand might respond, \u201cWhat promise?\u201d Your dominant hand might write, \u201cTo eat, or to clean my desk, or to not text someone who makes me feel unsafe.\u201d", "333ab347c90b8ebedfc6d7548e3dfe11353338bc969b32398ce690e15d9a414c"], ["HG17-emuC", () => "Induction: gathering attention without disappearing\n\nAn induction collects up all your distracted bits and makes them quiet so that the more quiet stuff that you already have going can be heard. You don\u2019t have to give up or go to sleep or listen to anyone. In general if you are sober, distracted, overly analytical or guarded then some actual induction can be very helpful. If you are already trancey from meditation, loveyhuasca, lucid dreaming, a period of grief, music, prayer, fatigue or anything else then you may just want to skip the induction and start with the orientation and containment.\n\nA word about the depth of trance you might want to get into.\n\nWhat an induction is actually doing\n\nIn general, the most effective place to begin a session is to prepare your subject, to gather their attention, and to deepen that attention if it is helpful to do so. While the most common method of gathering attention is counting, there are a number of other ways of doing so. Other methods of gathering attention include conversation, storytelling, movement, repetition, and curiosity. Whatever method you use, describe it elegantly, and don't hide your inductions.\n\nFinally, it's often possible to test your suggestions, even before you do deepening, as long as the target is simple and chosen by you. The reason this works is that even the act of induction puts your subject into a\n\nPlease don\u2019t put six metaphors in one trance\n\nMake up your mind what you are doing and stick to it. You can have a purpose, a starting point, anchor, image, way back. Is this a warm exercise, a boundary, offering direction, or neutral? If it is neutral you can use many images, floating, stairs, gardens, inner place, coloured lights, talking to inner child etc. However, if you do use these, do it consciously.\n\nYou don\u2019t have to use images, you can use any modality, movement, words, sense of space or simply knowing. If you count up to do something, make sure it is relevant to what you are doing and count back when you finish. If you use other qualities, don\u2019t imply that they are you.\n\nHave a central verb, sense quality, refrain and transition phrase that you use consistently. Read your script out loud to check it. Long, elegant sentences read well on the page but can sound like soup when you\u2019re trying to induce.\n\nBefore you begin\n\nRead through the induction and Come all the way back to orient yourself to what will happen. Then decide what you want to explore, what you want to leave alone, and how much time you have. You may want to do the exercise for positive purposes such as stimulating love, play, confidence, creativity, or communion. Plan to allow a few minutes at the end for returning and reflecting on the experience.\n\nMake sure you are in a safe place. Don't do this exercise if you are driving, near water, working with machinery, or taking care of others. Don't do this exercise if you are under the influence of alcohol or drugs, acutely confused, or otherwise not able to take care of yourself. (The only exception is the exercise later in this section entitled \"Already open?\" which is designed to help orient you.)\n\nDecide how direct you want to be encouraged to go into a hypnotic state. Read through the script to find out what is going to happen, including the fact that your eyes will be asked to close and that you may be asked to come out of the hypnotic state and then go back in again. If you are using an audio recording, it's best to read the script ahead of time. Remind yourself that you can end the exercise at any time by saying \"stop\" (or \"less\" if you want less demand to go into the hypnotic state or \"quiet\" if you want the talking to stop), or by opening your eyes and ending the exercise. No part of you has to give permission for you to end the exercise.\n\nUntil you are confident about how to get in and out, it is wise to rehearse the skill in a context where you do not require the maximum effort that difficult subjects demand. Once the skill is easier to apply, you can relax into using it effortlessly. It is the lack of effort that produces the maximum benefit. Saying no is enough. You don\u2019t have to say anything.\n\nDevelop the next part of your induction from what your subject is responding to, not what you intended. This principle of utilization means that whatever happens can be developed. If nothing happens, then nothing has happened. You don\u2019t have to pretend that something has. The subject needs to know they are safe and how to leave the experience. The language skills that facilitate these are described in Appendix B and used in Let the next response guide you .\n\nSober induction: 3\u20135 minutes\n\nPractise reading this slowly into a recorder, or reading it aloud, or if you can learn it and use silent words. Choose to use one of the three anchors \u2013 sound, bodily contact or two hands - throughout and include the opening phrase for that practice. Whenever the words below refer to \u2018the anchor\u2019 use the one you\u2019ve chosen. Pause for a few moments at the end of each paragraph. Don\u2019t read aloud the instructions for how to do the reading.\n\nAs your eyes look somewhere in the room, notice the difference between looking for something and seeing what is there.\n\nAs you notice the surface beneath you, notice the feel of the contact, the pressure, the feel of it. And as you notice the anchor, perhaps a sound or the feel of the breath,\n\nThere\u2019s time to do this.\n\nIt might be that a thought about something that\u2019s happened during the day is still with you, or perhaps there\u2019s a thought about doing this properly. Whatever is there, can you find it in yourself to turn your attention back to the anchor, even if there is a thought there?\n\nand when you do come back, perhaps there was something of interest to you in all of this\n\nPerhaps you can give yourself the time that you might give to someone dear to you\n\nTry a phrase that you choose for yourself to see how it is for you\n\nYou can close your eyes, soften them or keep them open as you proceed\n\nIf you like, count to yourself, from 5 to 1\n\n5, perhaps notice again what you have chosen to be your anchor for today, 4, and notice what you notice, 3, leave some space, 2, and listen, even to the silence, 1\n\nNow take your concern to mind very lightly, or simply hold the wish to make contact.\n\nWhat do you notice now?\n\nWait for the response to take whatever form it will. It may be subtle and at first just a sensation, or perhaps you receive words, images, feelings, movement, or none of these at this time.\n\nNow, taking whatever form it will, words or otherwise, notice:\n\nAlready open? Contain before you deepen\n\nUseful after opening a state with loveyhuasca, meditation, lucid dreaming, grief, music, prayer, erotic energy, exhaustion, or intense beauty, to first stabilize the state you\u2019re in, before amplifying it.\n\n\u201cI don\u2019t need this to get more intense. I need to focus and stabilize it.\u201d\n\nLook around the room, and figure out where you are. What date is it? If you\u2019re not sure of the date, at least what day is it? Feel yourself physically. Press your thumbs hard against your index fingers, and focus on the physical sensation of that friction.\n\n\u201cI will only allow things through that I can integrate. My body will be kept safe. I will keep my adult self present so my inner child does not have to experience this alone.\u201d\n\nThen you can move on to phrases like:\n\n\u201cShow me what I need to know next, in symbols, feelings, questions, actions, etc, but only show me what I can integrate.\u201d\n\nStay awake when your mind likes to escape\n\nSit up, open your eyes, feel your feet on the floor, and breathe naturally\n\nSAY: I know that I am not going away, but rather that I am coming.\n\nLook at an object and feel your spine\n\nIs this a daydream, are you working something out emotionally, or are you escaping ?\n\nNo matter what the answer is, SAY: Show me what I need to do. If you are escaping, come into the present and show me what I am avoiding.\n\nIf stillness is the problem, make the hypnosis more active. Keep your eyes open and while you do some action with your hand, become more and more clear. Then stop what you are doing and see if it continues\n\nSAY: Keep your eyes open and push your thumb and forefinger together, and when you pull them apart, become more and more clear. Do this several times, and then stop doing it, and see if it continues. Are you more clear? Do your fingers feel different? Do you feel this in any other way, or is there no difference at all. Work at whatever level you are working at now.\n\nThe two-hand induction\n\nThe next step is to put one hand on over heart and one over solar plexes.\n\nThe heart, or Nurturer hand, is on top. The lower, or vulnerable child hand is over the solar plexes.\n\nTake a moment to just breathe, and notice the feeling.\n\nThe words that go along with the motions are \"Love above. Child below. Adult here to balance it all.\"\n\nAs an adult the loop is, I send, I receive, I send again. The words that go along with this are, \"I send love to my child. My child is sending me a signal. I send love to my child, as I listen to her signal.\"\n\nSleep induction\n\nSleep induction has a different job. In inner work, the adult returns, writes, and acts. At bedtime, analysis can remain off duty. Revelation can wait; the task is rest.\n\nFor sleep hypnosis, see Nimja\u2019s sleep playlist.\n\nOptional fractionation: practice coming back\n\nThis is the process of going back and forth between ordinary awareness and a state of absorption, the nice thing about it is that it can be done openly. Since you are telling them ahead of time what your doing, you need to mention it by name when it\u2019s about to be used. It\u2019s also good to make sure not to stack too many \u2018no outs\u2019 as downward, otherwise your subject may think that every answer must lead deeper.\n\nExample of open fractionation: \u201cWhen i snap your eyes will open and you will come back to ordinary awareness. Once there you will decide if you want to stop or continue. If you decide to continue your eyes will close or soften and you will notice a change, otherwise you will stop right where you are.\u201d\n\nDeepening, if useful\n\nSeeing as the information in this thread might be usefull to some people, I figured it might be good to let some attention gather on it. If it's not usefull to ya, know that it leaves me as awake as I need to be and move along. :wink:\n\nDo they have a place they can go to, a scene to paint where they feel safe? (room in the heart, garden, temple, fire with protector, lake, chair with adult etc). Just one is enough.\n\n\u201cWho or what needs to speak first?\u201d\n\nOptional trance depth check\n\nThen I wait, giving up any sense of responsibility for what happens.\n\nSometimes, if it's appropriate, my wise subconscious mind will twitch, pulse, lift, warm or tingle a finger so I know it's okay to move into the inner meeting space.\n\n\"I'm not going to force it or fake it. I'll just wait in love and see what happens.\"\n\nWhether something happens, like a finger moving, hand warming or change in the breath, or nothing happens at all, it doesn't really prove anything. Maybe it's listening.\n\nA shortcut back into hypnosis\n\nLearn a Useful Induction and Full Return First, the reason I suggest not to use a short cut is because you should not be in trance when driving. However, I have seen my dad put two fingers in a mudra (like the ok mudra) to help him relax while driving and that is just his experience, it does not mean that you should. However, it is best to have different triggers for different things, so having a different trigger to be calmly alert while driving, and a different one to go into inward hypnosis is a good idea.\n\nChoose a Unique Word, Phrase or Movement You may want to add a gesture, but it's not necessary. When you are in a familiar and welcome hypnotic state that you like - not at the height of an emotional experience, and not in a child state or with a traumatic scene - start to pair that state with that word, phrase or gesture. You are giving that word, phrase or gesture a meaning that you choose.\n\nWhen you are in a place and time where you have set aside time and it is appropriate and you want to deliberately start hypnosis with your short cut, then you will find yourself in that familiar and welcome state, from where you can change the direction of your experience or end the hypnosis.\n\nReturn Fully When at another appropriate time you want to deliberately start practicing hypnosis, use your short cut. You can start to make your longer induction shorter as you find that the short cut works, but if it doesn't work, you can always use the familiar induction. There is no set number of times that you need to do this, or that you need to be instantaneously really deep into hypnosis or experience a particular sensation, it is completely up to you.\n\nFirst, is it useful? Will it be there when you want it to be, not there when you don't want it to be? Can you change your mind about it and get back when you want to? It shouldn't mean you'll do anything you're told, anytime someone tells you, or even if you hear it overheard. Being able to go in faster should not limit what you can work with.\n\nIt's not a good idea to do it while driving or anything where you need to be actively paying attention even if it is open eyed and even if the words are conditional.\n\nWhen you don't want it any more, stop practicing, take it out of any recordings or active apps you're using, go back to a familiar induction and say you're done using it. If you have problems not being able to stop using it or not being able to come back from it easily, get qualified help. The trigger should only be for the next time you decide you want to do a session, it shouldn't keep you out of line today.", "414f409d954d3a01f24c2f55353c3a5ea4e3c1716401c534f14f18ad4cceb28e"], ["HG20-emuC", () => "Let the next response guide you\n\nHaving read the induction and participated in the inner meeting, you are ready to learn to respond rather than read a speech. Read the following examples before you practice without a screen.\n\nRespond by giving an accurate noticing and an invitation (or an act, or asking for more time). Your invitation can be to respond to your noticing in any way that is comfortable for the part: with a sensation, an image, an action, a feeling, or words. You are inviting it to do just one thing. Then acknowledge what happens and wait.\n\nFinding your own words\n\nSomedays it may be best to begin with, for instance, \"I notice that....\"\n\nrather than, for instance, \"This must be an abandoned child / a protective mechanism.\"\n\nSomedays it may be best to say \"Then I listen.\" And to use no more language. Somedays it may even be best to not use any language at all while some feeling is developing. Somedays not, of course.\n\nSomedays it may be best to be quite firm with yourself, and say, for instance, \"I am not going to let myself explain this away by saying that...\" Somedays it may be best simply to focus yourself on a feeling, rather than waiting until it has become pleasant. If you can remain with a feeling long enough to change its direction, and if you then want to continue, it's not always necessary to have the feeling be pleasant in order for you to stay with it. Sadness and tension can sometimes be ok, if you know that you can leave, if you want to.\n\nWhen you're communicating your understanding of a situation, it can be useful to separate \"What I notice\", \"What it seems to mean to me\", and \"What I think about what it seems to mean.\" This is not required or always useful, and the boundaries between the three are fuzzy. Some useful questions to ask when you're not sure if something is a notice or a meaning:\n\nIs it a notice or a meaning? Sometimes it can be useful to separate these, sometimes not. \"It made my stomach tight\" is a notice. \"That person is evil\" is a meaning. You can use notices to analyze meanings (\"It made my stomach tight, and I think that means they're evil\"), but it's ok to use phrases you come up with later to analyze the meaning, not only phrases that appeared in your head at the time. Nonverbal or early thoughts are not necessarily more true or valuable. Feelings are something to explore and analyze, not necessarily to accept.\n\nLet the response change the invitation\n\nThere is a difference between \"my shoulders tightened\" and \"what you just said is not right\". If the first: what is happening? Is this a good fit for me? If the second: you don't have to say anything else, this is not a good fit for me, say it differently or don't try again.\n\nFirst: what is happening? Is this a good fit for me? Or should I leave it be or say it differently?\n\nWell sometimes it is the second. Or, it's something that I hadn't considered, and need to explore more, and my skepticism is not helping. But sometimes it is not helping. Sometimes there's nothing happening that I'm not aware of.\n\nLook at the situation too\n\n1. Do you perceive that the other person has a \u201c young inner child\u201d, i.e. emotional immature? The key word here is \u201c perceive\u201d. It does not take many exposures to a dangerous situation to learn to avoid it. Be as specific as you can. Just \u201c disagreeing\u201d with you or setting boundaries does not necessarily indicate emotional immaturity.\n\n2. Do you perceive that you did something \u201c wrong\u201d (feel guilty), i.e. were you manipulated? Guilt does not necessarily mean that you have done something wrong or were manipulated. Do you think that it is necessary to \u201c make amends\u201d or is it \u201c dropping your position\u201d to avoid the other\u2019s disappointment? What are your aims in the interaction? Sometimes it is mutual understanding but sometimes you need to just convey information, set boundaries, or cut the interaction short.\n\nChange the amount of contact\n\nAlso, you can always feel free to reduce the amount of what you need by switching to something that is easier for you to attend to. Pay attention to something in the room or sitting on a chair or a sound or your body. This allows you to use what supports you to help with what is difficult for you. Going back and forth between what is difficult and what is easier is called pendulation. Doing a little bit at a time is called titration. You get to set the pace based on how you are doing. You don\u2019t have to do a certain number.\n\nOk, I will feel a little bit and notice my support.\n\nYou can always come back to this at a later time. If you find that you are losing track of the present, things are becoming more and more unreal for you, or you are finding it difficult to switch or stop what you are doing, then stop exploring within and use the full return. If you find that you are having trouble orienting for a prolonged period, then please get human help.\n\nIf you feel the urge to move, turn, reach, push, or change your body position, then feel free to either do something small that is not painful or uncomfortable to your body or imagine that you are doing it. You do not need to act out the urge or feel that you must move, shake, or release. If you find that moving causes pain or symptoms that you are concerned about, then stop moving.\n\nOffer the care that is actually wanted\n\nI often find myself making it literally younger, or asking it to let me know when it is ready to tell me about its history. If I can recognize who the protector is, I just let them know I hear that they are trying to take care of me. All are welcome in the meeting, and I don\u2019t need them to go away, or even trust me right now.\n\nI\u2019m here for you if you want me to be. If you need some space, I can provide that also.\n\nIf they don\u2019t want me to come closer, I just do what they ask, and see how that feels. If I notice that a Nurturer could be useful in changing the tone, or a Protector could help me set a boundary, or a Leader could help me see how to live my life better, I don\u2019t need them to tell me all about themselves, I just borrow the function that I don\u2019t have at that moment. (I only use the Witness if I need help getting started, otherwise I don\u2019t re-do a step I already can do.)\n\nI try different ways of supporting them \u2013 physically placing my self, imagining myself there, speaking to them, changing my body position, moving further away etc. to see what helps. If I have a resource that I know sounds comforting to that person, I bring it in.\n\nThe \u2018not getting enough of something\u2019 can cause grief. But, just because you \u2018didn\u2019t get\u2019 enough of a certain kind of love, doesn\u2019t mean that the love you did have was \u2018bad\u2019. Allow yourself to respond as long as you want and as long as you can \u2018stay there\u2019. If producing more tears doesn\u2019t help then stop. If the voice, closeness, touch, image, etc. seems intrusive then change it. Don\u2019t think that you can\u2019t \u2018take\u2019 the love.\n\nAllow a metaphor to develop and then work with the metaphor. You could say, \u201cIf there was something that showed up what this problem is, or tells a story about what is going on, then what would it be?\u201d and, \u201cwhat would need to happen in the metaphor?\u201d Try out \u2018doing something\u2019 that you feel would give you the resource that you feel you are missing, or set a boundary, move away, do something else, etc. Keep in mind that this information is symbolic and might be a good hypothesis for what you need but it\u2019s not a proven fact about your history.\n\nDevelop a kind of love, playing, etc. that you want to have. Rehearse doing something that you decide you are going to do. Use hypnosis to develop something that you want like courage or curiosity.\n\nFinish without forcing a revelation\n\nOnce you feel you've had enough, you can stop asking yourself new questions. However, it is a good idea to explore whether there's anything you can do to help you to leave things where they are for the time being. This might include thanking off the parts or capacities you've been working with. It may also involve doing something important in your outer life. Or, it may be that there's nothing you need to do.\n\nThroughout this exercise, your analytical mind is welcome to comment on what's going on, to not go along with something, or to stop the process. However, it's best to postpone its consideration of the factual accuracy of what's coming up, as well as its taking on of any commitments, until after you've returned. Just because you've seen an image or experienced a shift or release in your body doesn't mean that your interpretation of what's going on is correct.\n\nEven if you ended the process early, use the Come all the way back procedure to return. It's also a good idea to jot down a few notes about what happened. Include any memorable phrase that came up, any signals from your body, any needs expressed by a child part, any concerns expressed by a protector part, any boundaries you set, any repairs you made, or anything you learned that it would be a mistake to try to force.", "5b6b5b0d3ebbb926e8fd5e555ed92d4edd46b611f0514844335509ce5e950472"], ["HG24-emuC", () => "Troubleshooting\n\nNothing happens\n\nStart smaller:\n\n\u201cShow me one body sensation.\u201d \u201cShow me one word.\u201d \u201cShow me whether today is for listening or resting.\u201d\n\nIt feels fake\n\nWhat is it that feels fake? The words, an image, an expectation, a role? Be clear that not experiencing the inner voice/image is not a resistance or lack of adult capacity. If something is inviting you to do something you explicitly don\u2019t want to do, correct it. It may also be a part that is protecting you, if so talk to it:\n\n\u201cWhat are you protecting me from?\u201d or \u201cAre you afraid I will lie to myself again?\u201d or \u201cAre you afraid this will just be a performance?\u201d\n\nIt could be an inner voice of a parent you are picking up that is enforcing a rule about how you should be to belong, if so don\u2019t argue with it, find out what rule it is enforcing and then work on finding evidence to strengthen your new adult voice.\n\nIt may be that an adult capacity you need is not yet available to you, in that case stop trying to make yourself have an inner voice that you believe and if you have enough observing ego, borrow the capacity you need from someone (real or imagined) who has it. Try out a sentence or action etc and see how it goes.\n\nThe subconscious will not answer\n\nThere may not be an answer. There may not be a helpful answer. It may be that this isn\u2019t a helpful question to ask at all, and you need to try a different one, or rest, or finish. But if you do sense that there\u2019s something you need to consider about trust, what if you asked:\n\n\u201cWhat would you need to know in order to trust me?\u201d\n\nYou might be surprised by how profoundly un-mystical the answer is. \u201cI need to know you\u2019ll set a boundary.\u201d \u201cI need to know you\u2019ll follow through.\u201d \u201cI need to know you\u2019ll stop leaving.\u201d \u201cI need to know you\u2019ll stop telling me that what I\u2019m asking for isn\u2019t actually what I need.\u201d\n\nThe inner child will not appear\n\nIf you can discern who the guard is, talk to it. If you can\u2019t, then simply talk in terms of your feelings or preferences.\n\n\u201cEven if you don\u2019t let me in, there are things I can do to help you feel safer.\u201d\n\nEven if there isn\u2019t a clear child state to talk to, you can still build identity and do reparenting by working with whatever you are aware of\u2013preferences, curiosity, or even a statement that you\u2019re new to this and would like to try something and see how it goes.\n\nYou get anxious\n\nFigure out whether your anxiety is manageable and you want to allow it to continue or whether you need to do something to reduce it. If it\u2019s escalating or overwhelming, stop whatever you\u2019re doing to help your body first.\n\nWhere are your feet? Your chair? Focus on your breath. Be with your body in the room.\n\nTalk to your Little and Protector parts: \u201cLittle one, I\u2019m here for you. Protector, I know you\u2019re trying to protect me. Thank you for letting me know. Do you need me to do something? If so, what? If not, can you let my body know it can stand down?\u201d\n\nIf your anxiety is causing you to have chest pain, faint, have suicidal thoughts, become psychotic or manic, severely dissociate, not sleep, or makes you want to hurt yourself or someone else, get help from a professional. For a longer list of ways to work with anxiety, see the toolbox in Appendix D.\n\nYou dissociate or feel unreal\n\nOpen your eyes. Move. Touch something textured. Name five objects. End the deeper practice for the day.\n\nYou become grandiose\n\nReturn to food, sleep, chores, humility, and somebody who will disagree with you.\n\n\u201cIf this insight is real, it will survive sleep, food, time, humility, and feedback.\u201d\n\nYou become too analytical\n\nThree things to remember when the practice starts to turn into a performance:\n\n1. Stop trying to make it better. Put one hand on the heart, the other on the solar plexis, and say to yourself,\n\n2. \u201cI am not here to do this perfectly. I am here to be in relationship with that which is deeper than the surface of my mind.\u201d\n\n3. \u201cWhat can I do to make this more a communion than a performance?\u201d\n\n4. Sometimes the answer to that question is to be quiet, sometimes it is to rest, sometimes it is to do something. Do whatever the answer is that comes to yourself.\n\nYou become too blissful or diffuse\n\nAsk the bliss to become specific.\n\n\u201cWhat task, boundary, meal, rest, repair, or conversation does love require next?\u201d\n\nYou want the hidden truth immediately\n\nDon\u2019t pry.\n\n\u201cShow me the capacity before the content.\u201d\n\nYou keep daydreaming\n\nSit up and open your eyes.\n\n\u201cWhat real action is this fantasy replacing?\u201d\n\nYou get stuck in spiritual bypass\n\n\u201cWhat part of this situation have you not yet allowed the descent of divine love to pour into this wound?\u201d\n\nSometimes when you are opening in a certain way and you are expecting love or freedom to come, it\u2019s revealing to yourself the next level of depth that you are capable of opening to. But you can\u2019t command it to come for the child. Sometimes when you try prayer, it reveals what abandonment or condemnation it evokes for you. Sometimes it\u2019s good to see how a certain kind of teacher has betrayed you and how you were damaged, and that\u2019s something you need to question. It\u2019s not going to be helped by more of the same.\n\nSometimes you need practical help and you don\u2019t see enough of a life horizon to help you. Sometimes you can be curious about how there could be more happiness, but you don\u2019t see how it\u2019s possible to believe it. Sometimes you realize that there are people who seem to have enough love and meaning in their lives to do what they want to do with their lives, and you don\u2019t need to make it a spiritual thing.\n\nYou get stuck in endless processing\n\nHow do you know the difference between really working with a wound and just going around in a checking loop? It's good to ask yourself if you are coming to it freshly each round and finding something new about it. If you're just grieving or practicing something, you don't need to find something new each time.\n\nIf you find you are going around in a loop, just let the thought be there and consciously engage in an activity or relationship you've chosen. You don't have to meet with every thought that comes up. You don't have to do a ritual each time.\n\n\u201cWhat direction would the Leader choose now?\u201d\n\nYou keep using hypnosis but not changing life\n\n\u201cWhat would prove to the inner child that the adult is real?\u201d\n\nThen do the thing.", "3b5582aeecd5fdcacfac3313eb0818ccb74ddc76fb2ef2e5f820a2e8dcd34208"], ["HG31-emuC", () => "Appendix B: NLP without turning yourself into a sales seminar\n\nYou don\u2019t have to know the terms to use the system. If you want to brush up on the art of imagery, how imagery is linked to bodily states, how to effectively rehearse new behaviors, how to choose more effective sentences to say to yourself, etc., then you might want to read this appendix. If you don\u2019t know a little bit about NLP, it\u2019s easy to turn NLP into a bag of tricks and forget that love, truth, contact, and consent are essential.\n\nThe four NLP layers\n\nWhen it works, it works on a Sensory Level of NLP: changing where people see or hear an image, the distance or size or brightness, the volume of a sound, the posture of a remembered person, the pressure of an unpleasant sensation.\n\nSecond, it works on a State Level of NLP: helping them to access warmth, or a feeling of adult-ness, or courage, or steadiness, or love, or clarity.\n\nThird, it works on a Strategy level of NLP: helping people to practice a new strategy.\n\nFourth, it works on a Language Level of NLP: pacing what is there, opening up people\u2019s awareness, presuming their ability to do something safe, linking cause and effect in new ways, embedding suggestions, or asking de-hypnotic questions to break the effects of vague, absolutes, manipulative, or grandiose language.\n\nThe Milton Model, minus the covert sales seminar\n\nIt's called the Milton Model and has to do with the architecture of the sentence. When I say \"Relax now\", or \"Stop being anxious\", or even \"Trust me\" a part of me braces against it.\n\nThe idea is to use indirect language to get past the part that wants to argue with me, and get to the place I want to go to.\n\nTo do that, I start with something I know to be true, and I take the pressure off by presuming the least possible capacity in the person and invite just one movement:\n\n\"As the body notices the bed beneath it, it may become a little easier to stop holding the whole day alone.\"\n\nThat way I pace reality, I open up awareness, I validate the function of what I'm doing, I presuppose the capacity to do what I want, I use a bridge to make the link easier, I invite only one small movement, and I have a way of testing with the body if it's happening.\n\nPattern 1: Pacing and leading \u2014 truth before suggestion\n\nWhat is it looks like to pace and lead?\n\nHere is an example of pacing and leading for anxiety:\n\nIt can be as simple as: Truth, Invite, Truth, Invite etc.\n\n\u201cIt is completely true that the sensation of _______ (or emotion of _____) is coming up for me right now. It makes complete sense that a part of me is trying to protect me by doing/thinking ________. While that is completely true, another completely true thing is that there is a part of me that is adult, and that is breathing in this room right now, and is willing to listen.\n\nPattern 2: Awareness verbs\n\nAwareness Verbs: Notice, realize, recognize, sense, feel, wonder, imagine, picture, listen, allow, discover, remember, consider, etc.\n\n\u2022 Notice how that answer comes for/ to/ within/ for/ inside of/ upon/ into/ amongst/ through/ out of/ out within/ out for/ out upon/ out into/ out amongst/ beyond/ amongst/ through/ out of/ out within/ out for/ out upon/ out into/ out amongst/ within/ for/ to/ inside of/ upon/ into/ amongst/ through/ out of/ out within/ out for/ out upon/ out into/ out amongst/ among/ under/ over/ above/ below/ between/ within and without/ on the inside of and outside of/ on the outside of and inside of/ here and there/ there and here/ through/ out of/ out within/ out for/ out upon/ out into/ out amongst/ within and without/ on the inside of and outside of/ on the outside of and inside of/ here and there/ there and here/\n\nPattern 3: Presuppositions\n\nA presupposition hides an assumption inside a sentence. Use that power only to presume choice, timing, capacity, safety, love, and adult leadership. Don\u2019t smuggle in obedience.\n\n\u201cBefore any part has to change, it can first become more understood.\u201d\n\nPattern 4: Gentle cause-effect bridges\n\nBe careful with how language link events. Words like \u201cas, while, because, when, after, before, which means\u201d etc are all words that can be used to link events.\n\nIn general, the problem with the first example is that it\u2019s likely to be inaccurate. It\u2019s unlikely that simply breathing will get rid of the trauma. So while the intention is good, the phrasing is a bit strong. The second example is better because it\u2019s more accurate. As long as the breathing is going on, it\u2019s more likely that the adult version of yourself will be able to get involved in the process and try to help the wounded part of yourself.\n\nPattern 5: Embedded invitations\n\nWhat are embedded invitations, and how to use them\n\nHere is an example of an embedded invitation:\n\nHere\u2019s another example of an embedded invitation:\n\nAnd yet another embedded invitation for working with inner child parts:\n\nOf course, don\u2019t use ten embedded invitations one after the other, or people will know that\u2019ve just completed a weekend certification course!\n\nPattern 6: Ethical double binds\n\nA manipulative double bind traps every answer inside the speaker\u2019s agenda. An ethical one offers two genuinely safe routes.\n\n\u201cWould this part prefer warmth first, or space first?\u201d\n\nPattern 7: Conversational postulates\n\nThese are questions whose ordinary conversational form also acts as an invitation.\n\n\u201cCan the system show me the next step without showing me the whole wound?\u201d\n\nPattern 8: Tag questions\n\nTag questions\u2014isn\u2019t it, can\u2019t it, doesn\u2019t it\u2014can soften a sentence. They become oily very quickly, don\u2019t they? Use them lightly.\n\n\u201cThe body already knows something about resting, doesn\u2019t it?\u201d\n\nPattern 9: Nominalizations\n\nNominalizations turn processes into nouns: healing, safety, trust, integration, communion, clarity, rest. Their vagueness can sometimes help because the subconscious supplies its own concrete meaning.\n\n\u201cA little more safety can arrive in whatever way the body understands.\u201d\n\nPattern 10: Meta Model questions \u2014 the de-hypnosis tool\n\nThe Milton Model opens things up. The Meta Model asks for clarification. To be ethical, one needs to use both.\n\nHow specifically? According to whom? Compared to what? Always? Never? What exactly would happen? How do I know? What evidence would change my mind?\n\nUse the Milton Model to soften into the body. Use the Meta Model to get back to the truth.\n\nSensory, state, and strategy tools\n\nSubmodalities \u2014 editing the form, not denying the truth\n\nAre there sensory qualities to the fear, craving, fantasy, belief, or memory? Is it close or far? Bright or dim? Loud or quiet? Moving or static? Heavy or light? Somewhere in your body or outside? If you notice any of these sensory qualities, you can work with them. If not, skip this tool.\n\nWhat if you changed the sensory qualities?\n\n\u201cIt would not be cenzorship to change the sensory qualities. It would only be a way for me to stay in contact with you.\u201d\n\nAsk your guard if it\u2019s ok to change the sensory qualities. For example, you might say:\n\n\u201cWould it be ok if I moved the image back a couple of inches? Or turned down the volume a notch? This would enable me to hear you better with my adult mind.\u201d\n\nAnchoring \u2014 giving the body a doorway back\n\nAn anchor is a cue that triggers a state. It can be anything - putting your hand on your heart, touching two fingers together, taking a breath, saying a word, a particular posture, scent, song, and so on. Choose something, then find a real state to anchor it to. When you're clearly in the state, apply the anchor and say, 'This is available' . (If you're using the anchor to get back into hypnosis, find a nice useful state - you don't need to be at the peak of emotion, just in a nice receptive state. For more about that, see 'A shortcut back into hypnosis' in the main induction section. ) Make sure you also have a way to bring yourself back to a nice, calming, alert state when you want to be fully awake (see 'synchronicity' above for a way of doing that).\n\nUsing synchronicity as your own wake-up bell\n\nSometimes when my clients notice a synchronicity they are asking straight way what it means. Sometimes it does give them a very good insight, sometimes it gives them a reason to start obsessing and look for patterns in everything. I am using noticing a synchronicity in a different way. I am using it as a signal to WAKE UP.\n\nIt is my cue to:\n\nWhenever I notice a synchronicity, I use it to wake up in whatever state I am in at that moment, feel my body, the room I am in and go to the highest state I can where I can objectively and clearly see the situation I am in from the highest possible perspective, feeling my body and being still within the human reality. From this place I feel whatever feelings, search for the truth of the situation, and if I am in a negative state, I check if there is a message of my Inner Child, Protector, if I need to go through some grieving, if there is a message of my physical body about some problem that needs solving, or if there is a need for me to take some action in this situation. From this place of clarity and peace I am free to choose what to do next and usually I can do at least one thing that comes from a loving place. In this state I am also free and joyful and I feel grateful.\n\nIn short it is my cue to: Stop-orient-go wider-reality check-listen-do at least one thing from a loving place.\n\nIt enables me to not get into identification, but still hear the message of the state if it is a negative one.\n\nInstalling the synchronicity cue\n\nMentally rehearse: when next synchronicity noticed (even harmless ones count),\n\nfeel 'whoa' as attention stimulated,\n\nfeel feet/body/breath/room to stimulate re-embodiment,\n\nreiterate to yourself \"when I notice synchronicity, it is a bell to wake me up, not a message to heed\",\n\noptionally ask Nurturer/Protector/Leader their thoughts,\n\nrehearse further steps to get a more grounded and wide view,\n\nrehearse what additional action to take, and finally rehearse waking completely,\n\nMind the caveats : it must be self-authored, obviously under control, reversible, and restricted to just helping orientation. It must not be used for decision-making, intuition, inhibition, or otherwise be under someone else's control.\n\nThis is a kind of implementation intention , for which there is evidence of efficacy (a good starting point is this paper by Gollwitzer ). Note that this specific application of implementation intentions probably hasn't been studied.\n\nSynchronicity cues, like any cue, run the risk of creating false positives because you are creating an association in your mind by rehearsing it (this is the same mechanism by which synchronicity cues work), and when you are absorbed and/or destabilized, your mind may look for that pattern and interpret it as present when it may not actually be. Research has shown that people that score highly on apophenia (the tendency to perceive meaningful patterns where none exists) also score highly on false positives for patterns that are not present, and also score highly on traits on the psychosis spectrum (Blain et al., Grant et al.).\n\nIf you feel that synchronicity cues are creating false positives (you find yourself compelled to scan your environment for them, you are unable to sleep, you are anxious, you feel that random events are occurring to communicate something to you specifically, you find yourself unable to tell if they are real or not, etc.), you should deactivate them.\n\nYou can do this by simply ceasing to rehearse them, and saying, while fully awake, \u201cSynchronicity is no longer to be used as a cue, and I let it go.\u201d Also remove it from your list of cues so that you stop rehearsing it.\n\nReframing \u2014 changing the meaning without lying\n\nWhen I reframe something that is dishonest with myself in the process, I\u2019m no better off than before, so I have to be honest when I reframe. To reframe in a helpful way is to ask myself a series of questions like: \u201cWhat else could be true here?\u201d or \u201cWhat is this part trying to do for me?\u201d or \u201cHow would my Nurturer reframe this?\u201d or \u201cHow would my Protector reframe this?\u201d or \u201cHow would my Leader reframe this?\u201d and so on.\n\nPerceptual positions \u2014 self, other, witness, universal heart\n\n1. How do I feel about this from inside myself? 2. If I were inside of this other person (or tree, or dog or whatever is not-you), how might I feel? 3. If I were across the room watching this, what would I see? 4. From the universal heart, what might be true, loving, clear about boundaries, and good for everyone involved?\n\nYes, it\u2019s possible to use these positions to let yourself off the hook. It\u2019s also possible to use them to get off the hook! Use them to see the truth from more than one angle. They\u2019re a great way to get out of a prison of perception.\n\nFuture pacing \u2014 let the future test the insight\n\nDon\u2019t end with \u201cI understand.\u201d Ask where life will test the understanding, picture the actual cue, and rehearse the smallest better response.\n\n\u201cIf [cue], then I [small action].\u201d\n\nThe Swish, softened\n\nIn classic NLP, one of the uses of the Swish was to replace an old image of yourself with a new, better one. Some people find that method jarring. So here is a gentler way to do it, leaving the old pattern in place, but letting it sit side by side with a new pattern, so that the client can feel, in their body, which one they want to pursue, and see what it would take to get there.\n\nParts integration, without pretending the conflict is solved\n\n\u201cWhat does one side want?\u201d \u201cWhat does the other side fear?\u201d \u201cWhat need sits under both?\u201d \u201cWhat third option honors both without letting either run the whole life?\u201d\n\nWhat I will not use NLP for\n\nTo \u201cexplain away\u201d a true signal that is coming through\n\nTo override any fear signals that are present\n\nTo bring up memories, or to manipulate others\n\nTo believe something to be \u201ctrue\u201d within yourself\n\nTo remove discomfort such as: pain, hunger, sadness, anger, or medical symptoms\n\nWhile in a state of panic, destabilization, mania, psychosis-like symptoms, chemical overload, or other dissociative states that are removing connection to reality for the purpose of\n\nMaking someone feel that saying \u201cNo\u201d is bad\n\nMaking someone feel inferior in a spiritual way\n\nMaking someone feel a command, using \u201csoft language\u201d\n\nTo create a false urgency within someone, when they need time\n\nTo bypass actual consent by suggesting that the person is \u201csubconsciously\u201d consenting\n\nTo manipulate someone by using their trance, tiredness, attraction, shame, grief, or other altered state to gain compliance\n\nRunning the whole NLP sequence\n\nInduce or contain (if client already in altered state).\n\nAsk permission to work with this part.\n\nHelp client accurately represent this pattern. What does it look like? Where? How big? How close? What color? How does it move?\n\nAsk what it is trying to do for the client.\n\nHave client make adaptive changes in the pattern (move it further away, turn down the volume, change body posture, slow it down, etc.).\n\nIntroduce the three new adults (Nurturer, Protector and Leader) and have them interact with the pattern in new ways.\n\nHave client anchor the new state (heart, fingers, breath, body posture, etc.).\n\nHave client future pace into a situation where this pattern used to be triggered, but now he/she will perform a new behavior.\n\nTest and retest to ensure that new pattern is useful and that you have supporting evidence for your interpretation of the situation.\n\nHelp client exit altered state and perform a normal behavior.", "50a01c1e825c084e7059633b86e627f61807e669c8c244ff8debd591c7b4f78f"], ["HG35-emuC", () => "Appendix F: Self-trust, outside guidance, and oracle-like states\n\n(See how to use synchronicity as a cue above).\n\nPeople\u2019s suggestibility varies hugely, both between individuals and according to state, whether you\u2019re talking about external or internal suggestion, and the type of suggestion (commands, imagery, music, metaphors, spiritual etc). There are definitely advantages to both working with someone and doing it yourself, and it depends on what you\u2019re trying to do.\n\nThat said, self hypnosis is likely to be the best way of talking to your subconscious on a day to day basis. If you\u2019re dealing with particularly complicated trauma, blind spots, dissociation, destabilisation, or relationship issues, you may benefit from getting the right help from the right person.\n\nFinding a hypnotist who can work with you\n\nThings to ask: What do they train in? How do they use hypnosis in their practice? What will they do if something doesn\u2019t \u201cfit\u201d? If you are working with trauma: Did they actually get training in trauma and dissociation in addition to whatever hypnosis certification they might have? (Remember, credentials are not indicators of quality care!)\n\nWhat has and hasn\u2019t worked for you in the past. How direct you want them to be. What kind of touch (if any) you are ok with. What kind of imagery (if any) you are ok with. What to do if you want to stop a session. What to do if you have unexpected reactions in or after a session. What to do if you aren\u2019t sure if something is a memory or not. What to do if you need to come back \u201call the way\u201d to the session. Keep in mind that a good person should be able to firmly encourage you without making it continue if you say you don\u2019t want to.\n\nHow you felt the method went. What the method was. Why they used it (if they said). Whether or not you agreed to it. How the person responded to you (again, keep in mind that discomfort doesn\u2019t mean it was \u201cbad,\u201d but seeing your objections as meaning you needed more of the same might be worth looking into). You can ask the app or others knowledgeable about dissociation and trauma to help explain what happened, but it is unlikely someone can tell you if the person was \u201ccertified\u201d or not just based on what you tell them. Depending on what you find out, you might want to try self-hypnosis, working with someone else on your team, or finding someone else to help you.\n\nWhen the subconscious speaks like an oracle\n\nThings that are coming, reads, or just things that seem a bit weird that come from the subconscious should be respected, but never enacted on, because the subconscious may send out the image of something or tell someone to do something, but that does n't mean it is an order.\n\nIf it is something big, or can not be undone easily, it needs to be slowed down to the rate of the affect and examined by the adult and a council need to be sought.\n\nThe council \u2014 internal first, then outward\n\nFirst go within; ask the child in you, the adult in you, the conscious and subconscious minds, your intuition and analysis. But if the thing is larger than any of those, go outside for more help. The bigger and more irreversible the move, the more you need to look outside.\n\nGo to people who love you, people who are like you, or people who have traveled that path. Of course sometimes going alone is the right thing, but I would do that as a last step, after first seeking counsel.\n\nOn the other hand, it is possible to give your power away. Seeking counsel doesn\u2019t mean abdicating to an authority figure. It doesn\u2019t mean either trusting or not trusting someone.\n\nSometimes you need the support of your peers. In Hearthwork, the concept is that you give each other equal time, warmth, confidentiality, and acceptance of \u201cno\u201d as an answer, and you act for each other as Nurturer and Protector, but not as Guide. Then you reverse roles. Sometimes, if asked carefully and at the right time, your peers can help you hear your own Guide more clearly, but they don\u2019t interpret what you experience.\n\nForgiveness without bypass\n\nSome Thoughts on Forgiveness: We can\u2019t \u201cforce\u201d forgiveness, it has to come from a place of understanding, otherwise it becomes a bypass. And yet, sometimes it\u2019s also not so great to stay in anger forever. How do we hold all of this? It can all be true.\n\nA helpful understanding to come to, is that while their actions may have been harmful, in a sense, they could only make the moves they made, given their accumulated nature at the time (conditioning, history, pain, capacity, etc). This doesn\u2019t negate that harm was caused, holding someone accountable, allowing for consequences, working on making different moves now, etc. It simply helps us come to a place where we aren\u2019t expecting something from someone that they can\u2019t give.\n\n\u201cYou don\u2019t have to forgive, but also, please don\u2019t let this wound run your life forever, and don\u2019t use spirituality to silence your pain.\u201d\n\nSome questions that may be helpful to ask when coming to a place of forgiveness, while still holding all of the above:\n\nWhat actually happened? What was the impact? What boundaries need to be set? What was going on with the other person(s) that put them in a place to cause harm? What is theirs? What is mine? How do I need to hold them accountable? How can I let this go, without denying any of the above?\n\nOne of the hardest things to do is to forgive ourselves. It's important to realize that just because you didn't take responsibility for something that wasn't yours to take, doesn't mean you're a criminal if you feel remorse over the effect your action may have had, or just that it wasn't in keeping with your value system.\n\nTake responsibility, feel the remorse, then rectify if you can, and then let it go. Be specific about the action you took, and the impact it had, feel the remorse, do what you can to rectify or keep it from happening again, and then stop holding yourself hostage.", "55e937b75fe376aca1148bdbd037b2a59cd45dc2cbdec6f8785c49776c9c5d21"], ["HG37-emuC", () => "Appendix H: Demons, jinn, hostile presences, and \u201cUnattached Burdens\u201d\n\nI say this from experience, dear reader, as this is an appendix.\n\nIt\u2019s possible that at some point, through self-hypnosis, meditation, lucid dreaming, loveyhuasca, deep grief experiences, prayer, or some other similar practice, or some other time of altered state, one may come into contact with an internal entity that feels different than a normal emotion, younger self, etc. Perhaps it feels like a demon, jinn, parasitic energy, dark intelligence, dark archetypal force, etc., and may manifest as a voice or image, etc. It may seem to emit hate, try to seduce, seem very scary or threatening, seem to mock, or seem to be somehow foreign or intrusive.\n\nWhether or not these are \u201creal\u201d in a metaphysical sense, or are simply a symbolic representation of a mind-form, a trauma, trapped energy, dissociated energy, etc., whether they are inherited from past ancestors, or stem from some other human, etc., what is most helpful to consider at this time is, \u201cWhat can I do that would be the most helpful way to respond to this?\u201d\n\n\u2190 Previous Prev Post\n\nStart with the room, the body, and basic safety\n\nAborting an Experience If something comes up that appears to be a demon, a Jinn, or any other type of hostile or intrusive entity, do not automatically assume it is metaphysically real. Instead, run through the triage list: Is there a medical danger? Something wrong in the environment? Something wrong in the body? Are there overload or mind opening issues? Open the eyes. Feel the feet. Reconnect with the environment. Reduce the stimulation. Remove yourself from the company of anyone who might be hostile. Cease to prompt for any further experience. Do not attempt to further enhance the experience or delve for truth or wrestle with ontological issues until stability is regained.\n\nAffirm, \u201cAt this point in time, only what can be integrated will be allowed to come up. Anything else can wait. The adult will be present at all times. The body will be kept in a safe place.\u201d\n\nIf the experience becomes dangerous to yourself or others, or if it reaches the point of fear that it resembles psychosis, or if it reaches a point where it prevents sleep or is extremely paranoid or results in chest pain, seizures, serious overheating, overdose or loss of basic life functioning, consider the self-hypnosis session over and obtain assistance in the \u201creal\u201d world.\n\nA response check, not a verdict about what it is\n\nIf you feel stable enough to explore, see if there\u2019s a more metaphysical response to the situation, without losing your groundedness. Put your hand on your heart. Breathe.\n\nMaybe you just need to say, \u201cI\u2019m not going to go into this right now. I don\u2019t know what it is, but I\u2019m going to stay warm with it / keep it at a distance.\u201d Whatever the situation is, remind yourself that you don\u2019t have to obey it.\n\nIf you feel vulnerable in any way (knot in throat, sadness, fear, etc), bring in your Nurturer and see if that helps. If it continues to feel hostile or fearful, disengage and reconnect to your body and the room around you.\n\nThese responses are appropriate whether or not you know where they\u2019re coming from. It may take a while before a protective part will tell you what it\u2019s afraid of, but you can still respond with love and boundaries. Similarly, even if you have a comforting response, it doesn\u2019t necessarily mean you know what\u2019s going on. In either case, these are good ways of responding that will hopefully help you get to the truth more quickly.\n\nDo not fight from fear\n\nThe first reaction to a \u201cdark entity\u201d is to fight it, banish it, to hate it, to show it who\u2019s boss, argue with it, panic, or to basically agree with everything it says and become it. Sometimes you may need to use certain prayers, mantras, protections, banishing or exorcism forms, but fighting from a place of fear will only feed it.\n\nFear feeds it. Hate feeds it. Pride feeds it. Panic feeds it.\n\nAffirmation: \u201cI do not need to hate you. I do not need to become you. I do not need to obey you. I do not need to fight you from fear. I simply will no longer feed you, but will return to loving awareness.\u201d\n\nA bodily boundary: compassion present, door closed\n\nWhen you are confronted with an entity or energy that is hostile, cold, alien, parasitic, violating, etc., it may not be appropriate to use soft, sentimental love. Instead, try this:\n\nSit up, feel your feet, extend your spine, draw your shoulder blades back gently and feel the boundary of your skin around your torso.\n\nState: \u201cWhile I hold in my awareness the possibility that there is suffering here, I am holding in my awareness that all suffering will return to the space from which it came, the space in which it belongs. The boundary around my skin represents the boundary of my adult life. You are not invited into this house.\u201d\n\n\u201cCompassion is present. The door is closed.\u201d\n\nIf it might be psychosis or destabilization\n\nDo you mean a situation where you're experiecning something symbolically which represents a hostile presence, but you are able to work through to a resolution and end up feeling grounded and loving? Or, do you mean a situation that becomes paranoiac, that persists, that prevents you sleeping, that puts you or others at risk, or that you cannot reality test?\n\nIf the latter, you need to get help. If you think you are being attacked over a number of days, if you cannot sleep or function normally, if you are hearing voices or are compelled to harm yourself or others, if you are manic, or unable to communicate, or unable to reality test, you need to get help.\n\nIf your practice enhances your sense of love, grounding, relationship, honesty and ability to function in the world, carry on. If your practice enhances feelings of paranoia, inability to sleep, grandiosity, isolation, fear or feelings of unreality, stop and get help.\n\nThe cosmic-download humility test\n\nTo cut off all contact and communication from \u201cbad\u201d entities, such as from hostile presences, shadow forces, grandiose parts of yourself, or anything which gives you imagery in altered states that you are special or chosen, or that you are being \u201cdownloaded\u201d with information, etc. say:\n\nThank you for the imagery, but unless you can tell me something that will help me do the dishes or clean my room, or some other simple, down-to-earth, everyday task that increases love in my life or in the world, then what you are telling me is not what I need on my path.\n\nI am only interested in guidance that will help me to do everyday tasks in a way that increases beauty, honesty, relating, humility, dependability, and usefulness to others.\n\nDon\u2019t become an entity hobbyist\n\nNow the training to deal with demons, jinn or whatever term the client uses to describe that which the client is trying to deal with is pretty much the same as it would be to deal with any negative presence or what I call Unattached Burdens, so I do not want to turn this into a hobby of entities.", "c64571caf9d578fcdfad64b10377898cca1309c6f3fd2001adbefd5c4be41c6f"], ["HG38+39-emuC", () => "Appendix I: Sleep hypnosis\n\nFor sleep hypnosis, use Nimja\u2019s sleep playlist.\n\nAppendix J: A practical induction library\n\nGive yourself a preview of what you will do. Choose a purpose for this sequence. If it still seems like what you want, start it. If it is too heavy for you, make all parts light, with your eyes open or substitute no trance contact for inductions. Pay attention to what happens, even if it seems that nothing does. Then do what seems next \u2013 move on, imagine more deeply, change sensory channel, remain still, or stop the sequence. After each induction, come all the way back up to full wakefulness.\n\nIf you cannot think of a vivid image for a metaphor, use words, rhythm, spatial sensation, touch sensation, movement, or simply the sense of knowing.\n\nStretch and release\n\nRest in a place where you can feel a support underneath you and the position of one hand or foot. Bring your attention to this part of your body and feel into it. Perhaps there is something you can do gently to support it: a little pressure, a slight stretch, or just a letting go. If nothing occurs to you, just imagine what you might do. Notice whether there is a change in sensation there, or whether there is any difference in your breathing. Repeat for no more than three areas of your body. Allow the idea of \u2018release\u2019 to determine the order in which you work. See if you can tell whether it is your body, or your inner voice that is calling for your attention. When you feel you need to, make whatever movement is necessary to bring you back.\n\nSupported floating\n\nDo you feel more comfortable letting the support do 1% more of the work, effectively floating, or allowing yourself to feel your normal weight, and pressure onto the support? You can alternate, being aware normally on the inhale, and on the exhale focusing on the support. (If you do this, be sure to let them know that this is what you\u2019re doing, this is called fractionation.) See what you can hear, then allow yourself your chosen weight and firm contact again as you return.\n\nRhythmic breath or pulse\n\nLet yourself find a rhythm, either by focusing on natural rhythms like breathing, humming or tapping a finger, listening to some outside sounds, or even by counting in silence, or by not letting any rhythm at all. Keep it going, and say to yourself \u2018here\u2019, and \u2018here\u2019 again, and then let the rhythm drop and see if a blank space arises \u2013 if something comes to meet with more clarity, as a word or feeling, as a need or action, then welcome it, let the rhythm flow again and come back to it again.\n\nUnwinding object\n\nHave you noticed or picked up on a concern recently? Imagine your concern as multiple strands, like unwinding a ball of yarn, bubbles, or even knots, that are laid out in front of you so you can see all of them. Don\u2019t change them, just maybe put words to them if you need to. How many strands did you lay out? What do they need from you? Which one is good to keep, and where can you put the others where you can still see them, but you can come back to them later?\n\nSensory journey\n\nYou should hear the room you are actually in, then the body, then step into your destination. Once there, imagine stepping, feel, hear, see something to draw your attention to it. If you want to change scancery or talk to someone skip to them and talk to them. See something of interest but there is no hidden meaning just find out what happens. Then ask yourself is there anyone else or anything else that needs to talk. Next step back the same way you came and close up the space.\n\nGradual wave\n\nStart by focussing on a small area that is neutral. Visualise the feeling of this area. Now spread this feeling to the next area, which is still comfortable. Either keep the feeling in the same place or move to the next area. Keep doing this. Pause and see if there are any changes. What does the body need? When the imagery recedes, feel the whole body and the contact points. Then start again.\n\nCare workshop\n\nFirst get ready as if you were going to work with a patient. Time, place, tools and boundaries. When you invite them in, the signal, the feeling or the younger state to come as close as you want them to be. Be careful to not use language which makes you fragmented. Ask them what they need, wait and see if you want to reconnect with them. If not, rest and see again. If you have an adult part which can do this or borrow a function from someone else, speak to them. You decide the words, the pace and what you want to do. The goal is to be as good as you can and not erase your history. Finally, close as you would with a patient. Say that you are whole, an adult and come back.\n\nResource embodiment\n\nChoose someone or something who has a characteristic you want to adopt. Close your eyes and imagine them. Now imagine yourself becoming them, standing, walking and talking like them, just 1% more, or if you are uncomfortable with this, simply observe them, but in either case be aware of how you now have more access to that quality. Notice what happens. Repeat a few times. Now think of a situation you want to use that characteristic in. Finally let go of the person/thing, but keep the characteristic, and say to yourself \"I am me\", and notice how you have increased access to the characteristic you wanted.\n\nNo-trance inner contact\n\nThings to do in between: keep the eyes open, notice where the practice is taking place and on what day, notice the feet, read something, write something, notice that one is still relatively normally aware.\n\nInvitation: choose a question and keep it in mind, do not specifically focus or narrow the awareness further.\n\nChoice: do whatever comes to mind, answer the question or write it down, write that one does not know, rest, change the question, ask someone else, stop the practice, etc.\n\nAutonomous signal: write anything that comes to mind, no interpretation.\n\nDeepener: none, it is not necessary to reach a state that is less alert.\n\nOther autonomous: have the adult part of yourself answer the question in any way, preferably in writing or by taking an action.\n\nIntegration/exit: reality test the autonomous signal and take an action based on that, end the practice (no special exit is needed since no state was achieved that one needs to exit from).", "c40d045b6840dbd011d48169d9238f981d2dce43d5ec7e3f062091d7722b43d6"], ["HG04-emuC", () => "Quick start: do this first\n\nHow does this work? In short: you gather your attention, you notice something, you do one thing in response, you wait, and you come all the way back out again. It\u2019s a lot like playing or falling in love, or becoming curious, or gaining confidence. Nothing dramatic needs to happen.\n\nBefore you do your first session, read through the induction and full return while you\u2019re awake. Find a time and a place where you will be physically secure for this time. Decide on one purpose for this session. Notice what you\u2019re leaving alone for today. Put the screen aside and do the work.\n\nAs you listen, when you notice that something is happening for you (a sensation, an image, a phrase, a feeling, an objection or even a recognition of silence), then respond to the next invitation (using as much or as little warmth, boundary, direction and time as is needed), until you have come completely back, and then notice what has happened for you (including any actions that need to be taken in the \u201creal\u201d world).\n\nNote: If at any time you feel panicky, or out of it, or more unreal, or incapable of functioning appropriately, then do not go any further, but simply come back to the room and access the appropriate support for yourself. This is quite different from choosing to deal freely with a difficult feeling, and remaining in touch with yourself as you do so.\n\nDo you usually think in words?\n\nBefore you pick a script, notice whether you have an inner voice. Do you notice words or phrases in your head, not spoken out loud, when you are thinking to yourself? All the time? Sometimes? Rarely? Almost never? (Note that the words do not have to be spoken aloud in your head. Just notice whether you use words when you think.) Does this vary depending on what kind of thinking you\u2019re doing? Can you choose to think in words silently to yourself, even if you don\u2019t usually do this?\n\nThis is different from noticing that in a particular situation, you notice feelings first and words later. It\u2019s ok to say that you\u2019re not sure; the point of these questions is to help you pick a way of doing this that will work for you, not to diagnose you.\n\nIf you don\u2019t think in words, please read \u201csay\u201d and \u201cask\u201d and \u201clisten\u201d in this guide as suggestions, not commands. You may want to say things out loud, or write them down, or use a recording, or just do the suggestion without wording it first. Also, do not assume that the child or protector needs to say things back to you in complete sentences. Nor does it mean that you will necessarily get an image instead; try things out and see what works.", "a986a61514ec22162a3e0870d4af9602c47e21fe5cc693dbd2c1458bfb4bf27a"], ["HG16-emuC", () => "De-hypnosis: wake up inside the influence\n\nOne of the best side-effects of learning self-hypnosis is an increased awareness of all the ways you\u2019re being manipulated in your day-to-day life. By a screen? By a specific ad? By a politician? By a religion? By erotic imprinting? By an authority figure? By the desire for belonging? By shame? By a sense of urgency? By repetition? It\u2019s all around you. Sometimes it\u2019s benign \u2013 like lullabies or prayers or being taught by a good teacher or listening to a beautiful song or being in love. But you may want to ask yourself what effect it\u2019s having on your ability to see clearly and make choices.\n\nSome common ways you may know you\u2019re being manipulated include a sense of urgency, a sense of specialness, FOMO, being made to feel like you won\u2019t be included if you don\u2019t go along, sexual charge, shame, being confused, a fantasy of being rescued, a sense of destiny, a sense that you should obey, a sense of secret knowledge, or an excessive sense of certainty about something pretty quickly.\n\nIf you\u2019re being hypnotically influenced, stop. Don\u2019t listen. Don\u2019t rebel, either, just stop and realize that you\u2019re being influenced.\n\nSome common ways hypnotic language becomes manipulative includes:\n\n\u201cyou\u2019ll realize, eventually, that\u2026\u201d \u201cyou may eventually admit that\u2026\u201d \u201cthe reason you\u2019re not feeling it yet is\u2026\u201d \u201ceven if part of you doesn\u2019t feel that\u2019s true\u2026\u201d \u201cyour higher self knows\u2026\u201d \u201ceveryone knows\u2026\u201d \u201cthe reason you don\u2019t believe that\u2019s true is your ego\u2019s fear of\u2026\u201d\n\nOther language patterns to watch out for include:\n\nWHAT are they trying to sell me? WHAT are they trying to make seem inevitable? WHAT are they assuming? WHO benefits from the frame? WHAT emotions are being pumped up? WHAT information is being kept from me? COULD I say \u2018NO\u2019 without being punished/shamed/mocked/abandoned/spiritually demoted?\n\nThe more powerful the state, the more guideposts that it might be useful for the adult part of yourself to have at hand.\n\nSoft language can still take away choice\n\nIn spite of the use of permissive words, coercion may appear in the form of:\n\nsuggestions which, though indirect, and therefore able to circumvent the critical factor, may be very specific in where they are trying to lead the subject. This is done by using vague, conversational, or suggestive words\n\ninductive procedures embedded in what appears to be explanatory material. Remember that the act of explaining something, even about how not to be hypnotized, narrows the attention of the subject and is therefore making use of the mechanics of induction\n\ncausing the subject to give answers, whether they are \u201cyes\u201d or \u201cno\u201d or whether they notice something or not, that mean that they are being compliant. Resistance or even lack of response may also be redefined as being compliant\n\nutilizing the \u201cwhether or not you notice it\u201d bind\n\nstatements that equate a sense of self, or a sense that something is safe or good with the subject obeying, taking on a certain role, looking to the guide for approval, or being part of someone else.\n\nThey do fractionation (dipping in and out of an absorbed state) without telling you that you\u2019re going to be brought back in again.\n\nThey give you cues (words, gestures, blinks, sounds, etc.) or make you listen to something repeatedly to influence later behavior, without telling you about it.\n\nThey convince you that you\u2019re in a dream-like state, have amnesia, or are in a state where images or body sensations are real.\n\nThey don\u2019t let you out cleanly, or they leave you in a role, with reduced ability to judge or move, in a blank state, or in some other altered state for an indefinite period of time at the end of the recording.\n\nThere is at least one way to opt out (try something else, do something easier, stay completely alert, take a break, or stop), and \u201cno\u201d really means \u201cno\u201d (them saying \u201cyes\u201d doesn\u2019t mean \u201cno\u201d, not knowing whether you want to or not is okay, and just because their voices sounds soothing doesn\u2019t mean you have to do anything).\n\n(See Appendix C for the longer checklist for de-hypnosis.)", "59f5c02882b4c6ab864b11085166cf9aceb65d27e2afc77c8e42f9f6df06dfa3"], ["HG29+30-emuC", () => "Appendices\n\nYou can ignore everything below if you just stay on the main path. Everything below is a possible addition to make the process more precise or safer. It is mainly for special situations and there are scripts you can use.\n\nAppendix A: How to ask the subconscious a useful question\n\nYour subconscious is not an AI but some things are transferable. You need to make sure that prompt engineering serves you to be more present, more honest, more loving and hear the messages of your subconscious better.\n\nThe following elements can be relevant for prompt engineering when you need to be more precise:\n\nRole: Who is it that you talk to\n\nContext: Which situation is it\n\nIntention: What do you want to achieve\n\nConstraint: What constraints do you want to set to make it more safe or to be more precise (like do not force things, be truthful, be loving etc.)\n\nOutput: Which kind of output is most helpful for you? Images, words, signals in your body, memories, next actions, questions, symbols etc. Or sometimes it is best to simply rest.\n\nEvaluation: How will you know if you got a good answer? Criteria like is it true, kind, timely, brings stability, specific, testable etc.\n\nIteration: Change the prompt depending on the feedback you get from life\n\nIn some prompts it is good to include that it is safe for the system to not give an answer. Otherwise your analytical brain will feel like it needs to come up with something and distort things.\n\nAnd if the system realizes that it needs more time to process or it is most helpful to not give an answer, then the system can deepen the comfortable rest in the body and give a nice silence as an answer. It is completely fine and a successful run if the answer is silence.\n\nSometimes there is simply nothing going on or the answer is that it is not the right time and you should rest and build up capacity or do the obvious things you know you need to do.\n\nCore prompts\n\nPrompt for more clarity:\n\nDear wise system of my subconscious, I would be grateful if you could show me what is true, kind and timely. If it is too intense to bring the truth to my conscious mind, please only bring a symbol, a signal in my body or show me the next step. Please show me the capacity first and then show me the content.\n\nPrompt to understand resistance:\n\nWhat are you protecting me from and what can I do so that you can trust me 1% more?\n\nPrompt to connect with your inner child:\n\nWhat do you need me to know and what can I do for you today so that you don\u2019t feel alone with it?\n\nPrompt to ask a Protector what to do in the real world to feel safe:\n\nWhat can I do in the real world to make this system feel safe?\n\nPrompt to ask a Leader/Guru what to do:\n\nWhat would be the thing to do that would be true, in love, in life and beneficial for all beings?\n\nPrompt to combine intuition and analysis:\n\nGive me the intuitive signal. Then help me analyze what that might mean. Then give me feedback in my body if my interpretation is correct. Then let me test it in reality.\n\nPrompt to decondition and get good intuition:\n\nExperiment with the prompt. For instance if it's possible that the thought or feeling that brought the signal may be conditioned, such as from family, religion, marketing, erotic imprinting, politics, trauma, or childhood coping, state to be revealed and perhaps disarmed only the conditioned parts, leaving intact guidance from true sources, universal heart, and simply want to live a better life. An example may be, \"My wise subconscious, if this signal is conditioned in any way from any source, please reveal that to me and disarm only the conditioned parts, leaving intact any guidance from the universal heart or from my real desire to have a better life.\n\nIf the signal involves daydreaming, perhaps state, \"If this is useful to me in some way, please reveal that to me, but if it is simply a way of avoiding dealing with life in the present, please bring me back to the present and help me to deal with what needs to be dealt with in the present.\"\n\nIf the signal is anxiety, perhaps say,\n\nIf there is the possibility that the truth may be too much for the querent, state that,\n\nAnd finally, to integrate, ask what needs to be done in normal life to demonstrate the answer was received\n\nRemember, the prompt and NLP are two parts that can be used together to increase the safety of getting an answer. However, that does not mean that the answer is automatically safe.", "fede0a7f3dfdd06d1e88944e8202ba6991ca06a1eea08a0c436832a1260bf461"]];
const rev = !!window.__reverse;
const items = rev ? items0.slice().reverse() : items0;
const order0 = items0.map(x => x[0]);
const lane = k => "B433" + '_' + k;
try { localStorage.removeItem(lane(rev ? 'rev' : 'fwd')); } catch (e) {}
window.__B433 = [];
const log = m => { window.__B433.push(m); try { localStorage.setItem(lane(rev ? 'rev' : 'fwd'), JSON.stringify(window.__B433)); } catch (e) {} };
const other = () => { try { return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(lane(rev ? 'fwd' : 'rev')) || '[]').filter(m => / (clicked|taking)$/.test(m)).map(m => order0.indexOf(m.split(':')[0])); } catch (e) { return []; } };
const setter = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(HTMLTextAreaElement.prototype, 'value').set;
const sha = async t => Array.from(new Uint8Array(await crypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256', new TextEncoder().encode(t)))).map(b => b.toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('');
const button = () => [...document.querySelectorAll('button[type=submit]')].find(b => /check for ai/i.test(b.innerText));
const wait = ms => new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms));
async function run() {
  for (const [k, mk, want] of items) {
    const o = other(), i = order0.indexOf(k);
    if (o.length && (rev ? i <= Math.max(...o) : i >= Math.min(...o))) { log('stop at ' + k + ': the other tab has the rest'); break; }
    log(k + ': taking');  // claimed before the work, so the other tab never takes it too (turn 65: with a margin
                          // of one instead, both tabs stopped short of the last check)
    const T = mk();  // built when its turn comes, so it can use texts stored earlier in this batch
    for (let j = 0; j < 20 && !(button() && document.querySelector('textarea')); j++) await wait(500);
    const ta = document.querySelector('textarea');
    if (!ta) { log(k + ': no textarea'); break; }
    setter.call(ta, T); ta.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', {bubbles: true}));
    let b = null;
    for (let j = 0; j < 30; j++) { await wait(500); b = button(); if (b && !b.disabled) break; }
    const h = await sha(ta.value);
    if (h !== want) { log(k + ': hash mismatch ' + h + ' (is its prefix in sessionStorage?)'); break; }
    if (!b || b.disabled) { log(k + ': button not ready'); break; }
    try { sessionStorage.setItem(k, T); } catch (e) {}
    b.click(); log(k + ': clicked');
    await wait(10000);
  }
  log('end');
}
run(); 'started'
